{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1086625-antagonist-advice-bloodlines-for-the-four-horsemen","id":1086625,"title":"Antagonist advice- bloodlines for the four horsemen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-02T07:31:43-07:00","id":1086625,"title":"Antagonist advice- bloodlines for the four horsemen","content":"So!<br /> <br /> In my game, the major antagonists are going to be a coeitre of vampires basing themselves on the four horsemen of the apocalypse. The question is, what bloodlines are best for them?<br /> <br /> Morbus for Pestilence, obviously, and Kallisti works for War. But I can't really find anything for Famine, and there are enough necromancy ones that I am unsure for Death. So, various vampire fans, does anyone have any ideas? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:52:51-07:00","id":1086632,"title":"","content":"I don't get why anyone would include &quot;antagonists&quot; in Vampire, having a clearly defined enemy defeats the purpose of the game.<br /> <br /> Though I would suggest Sangiovanni for Death and maybe a particularly starved-looking Nosferatu for Famine, with a backstory to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 05-02-2017, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:50:09-07:00","id":1086656,"title":"","content":"Burakumin (1st ed. Nosferatu) for Death. <br /> Any Gangrel or Ventrue for War (Animalism can be used to immediately put individuals or groups into a killing rage) but Children of the Morrigan (Gangrel) or Canda Bhanu (Ventrue) may be appropriate due to the warlike nature of those bloodlines. The Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse is a Christian theme and those bloodlines are not.<br /> Famine is a bit harder to put into a bloodline because disciplines don't manufacture those effects directly but Cruac can. Alternatively Animalism can be used to summon swarms of locusts or other vermin to destroy food/grocery stores, shipping and trucking lines to induce famine. <br /> The thing is, there are no bloodlines that specialize in Animalism except the Melissidae and that's to reinforce hive mentality. I would probably homebrew something along those lines. But I also wouldn't use the Morbus for Pestilence either. I'd use a Gullikan (Daeva) AND a Brothers of Ypres (Gangrel) because working in conjunction, they could poison a lot of people very quickly and have them simultaneously addicted to the poison of choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:05:43-07:00","id":1086684,"title":"","content":"The white horseman is probably more accurately translated as Conquest than Pestilence. The New American Standard translation says this about him:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then I saw when the Lamb broke one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures saying as with a voice of thunder, \u201cCome.\u201d I looked, and behold, a white horse, and he who sat on it had a bow; and a crown was given to him, and he went out conquering and to conquer.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Going by this passage, I would suggest an En, an Architect of the Monolith, an Icarian, or maybe a Bron as the white horseman. However, this later passage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were given power over a fourth of the earth to kill by sword, famine, plague, and by the wild beasts of the earth. </div> </div> </div>is the one usually drawn from to justify identifying the white horseman as pestilence. Going off of this, I would keep Morbus as the white horseman, who kills by plague, or maybe Iltani. If you're going this route, you'll want the pale horseman to kill by the beasts of the earth, so something with a strong connection to animals and animalism. Dead Wolves, Hounds of Acteon, or Melidsadae. The red horseman kills by the sword, which could be just about anything, but Spina, Order of Sir Martin, Moroi, or even Khabit would all be appropriate. If you want to focus less on the &quot;kills by the sword&quot; and more on the theme of warfare, weirdly enough I think the Brothers of Ypres would be one of the most thematic choices. There's really no Bloodline that kills by famine so you're going to have to get creative with the black horseman.<br /> <br /> For the black horseman, NASB has this to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When He broke the third seal, I heard the third living creature saying, \u201cCome.\u201d I looked, and behold, a black horse; and he who sat on it had a pair of scales in his hand. And I heard something like a voice in the center of the four living creatures saying, \u201cA quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius; but do not damage the oil and the wine. </div> </div> </div>So he is less focused on outright starvation than often presented in pop culture, and more on the management of scarce resources. I would actually use a Shepherd for him, since their whole schtick is careful management of kine herds. Alternatively, you could go ironic with it and make the black horseman a Macellarius. Focus on the horseman's own gluttony instead of the famine he causes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:07:13-07:00","id":1086817,"title":"","content":"The whole sort of Hollywood type of Four Horseman of the Apocalypse isn't very accurate. Lots of names would be more appropriate than the &quot;known&quot; ones. White horse rider, king, prince, or archer. Red horse rider, warrior, knight, swordsman. Black horse rider, judge, merchant, moneylender. Pale horse rider, death, or hellbringer. Each list would be for one horseman. All boring unless you use a language other than your native one. I could see something there if you said it in German or something like that. I assume these people had real names at some point. They could be John, Paul, George, and Ringo. I wouldn't get hung up on names at all.<br /> <br /> As for bloodlines, I would look at the abilities of the horsemen as a whole and separate them into four groups. It isn't really clear whether they are supposed to act singly or as a group, so I would not stick with individuals must have this ability either.<br /> <br /> Conquer could be Dominate<br /> Taking peace would be some ability to incite rage or madness that tends to lead to violence<br /> You would have to decide whether to take wheat for a penny, etc. literally or the more likely intended figurative meaning. Either way you have something losing value. I can't think of any way to handle it no matter the interpretation. Some people consider that part about truth and goodness becoming worthless rather than literal resources. I don't know if that helps. I would skip that one and try to tie something in the end if I can.<br /> Kill with a sword could be something physical or dealing out damage<br /> Kill with hunger would tend to be something that causes hunger or starvation<br /> Kill with death likely means disease so that would probably be a Morbus<br /> Kill with beasts is likely Animalism<br /> <br /> Given the subject matter, it would not be out of line to include some Theban to cover more obscure abilities.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, the Book of Revelations is somewhat unusual in supposedly being a later book (authorship and date uncertain) but much more vague in places or appearing allegorical. Nobody agrees what the thing means or how to take it, more so than normal for the entire text, obviously there are varying opinions throughout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T17:58:35-07:00","id":1086906,"title":"","content":"These are all good and useful ideas! Thank you everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:58:50-07:00","id":1088704,"title":"","content":"I second the Icarian suggestion (if you go with the Conquest theme). They're associated with the Lancea, so there's a shortcut to the religious aspect of the four horsemen aesthetic, and, more than that, they're kind of the bad kids of the Lancea and it's easy to see one of them as obsessed with reclaiming the name of the bloodline and dominion over the covenant. In terms of powers, they're not terribly original, but I do have a soft spot for them as one of the main antagonists of my last campaign was an Icarian. Plus, they're ventrue and you can never go wrong with ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T08:05:58-07:00","id":1088758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1086625-antagonist-advice-bloodlines-for-the-four-horsemen?p=1086656#post1086656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burakumin (1st ed. Nosferatu) for Death.<br /> Any Gangrel or Ventrue for War (Animalism can be used to immediately put individuals or groups into a killing rage) but Children of the Morrigan (Gangrel) or Canda Bhanu (Ventrue) may be appropriate due to the warlike nature of those bloodlines. The Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse is a Christian theme and those bloodlines are not.<br /> Famine is a bit harder to put into a bloodline because disciplines don't manufacture those effects directly but Cruac can. Alternatively Animalism can be used to summon swarms of locusts or other vermin to destroy food/grocery stores, shipping and trucking lines to induce famine.<br /> The thing is, there are no bloodlines that specialize in Animalism except the Melissidae and that's to reinforce hive mentality. I would probably homebrew something along those lines. But I also wouldn't use the Morbus for Pestilence either. I'd use a Gullikan (Daeva) AND a Brothers of Ypres (Gangrel) because working in conjunction, they could poison a lot of people very quickly and have them simultaneously addicted to the poison of choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Daeva - Sakti Pada discipline. Forgot the name of the bloodline though. Some crazy good stuff for war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}